WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
Rapping up the week on Tesla's short time, episode 537, Patrick here in Vancouver,

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.600
its July 10th, 2026. Let's close out the week with today's Tesla news.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:18.100
Tesla's patented breathing glass roof could cut hot weather range loss by actively managing cabin

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:24.100
climate where the sun hits hardest. Yesterday, the show covered fresh robo-taxi developments.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.780
Today, that thread moves forward with a limited unsupervised service now running in Miami.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.280
Using a small number of vehicles, the operation is testing real-world driverless rides in Florida,

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:42.200
while only a handful of cars have been observed so far. At the same time, a bill in New Jersey

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:48.180
targets vehicles without a human driver and would ban Tesla robot taxis from operating in the state

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:54.320
if it passes. The measure would rank among the stricter state restrictions on unsupervised ride

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:59.780
hailing. Broughter uncertainty remains at both state and federal levels around approval

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:06.160
timelines and vehicle requirements that differ by jurisdiction. Tesla's ability to expand beyond

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:12.760
the Miami test depends on clearing those gates. While regulators weigh in on autonomy, Tesla is

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:19.100
still filing patents that quietly improve the vehicles themselves. The company has filed for a perforated

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:25.420
multi-layer glass roof that turns the pain into an HVAC diffuser. Conditioned air flows through a

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:32.240
gap between layers and exits through holes with 1-6% perosity. Laser etching and edge polishing

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:38.280
keep the holes from cracking the glass. Optional honeycomb walls and staggered pains let engineers

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:45.140
tune the design for specific noise frequencies. Testing in 104-degree weather showed mean compressor

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:54.240
power dropping 7.4%. Over a 5-hour drive, that saving recovers roughly 2.8 miles of range on a 75

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.420
kilowatt hour battery. The same approach could apply to windshields and the gap thickness can be varied

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:06.680
across the pain. Tesla directed followers to its website to schedule a cyber truck test drive.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:12.440
The promotion aims to let potential buyers experience the vehicle's unique features first hand.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:19.140
The call to action links directly to Tesla's standard drive scheduling page. The post appears on

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:26.120
the corporate Tesla account alongside other current model highlights. No specific test drive locations or

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:32.320
inventory details were included in the message. The effort aligns with ongoing efforts to increase

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:38.700
in-person exposure for the vehicle ahead of wider availability. On the competitive side,

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:45.360
Australia's top 7 electric vehicles in recent sales are all Chinese made, including Shanghai

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:53.380
built Teslas. BYD and MG have gained ground through strong pricing and ready availability. Tesla models

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:59.840
from the Shanghai plant still sit inside the top 7, even as domestic Chinese brands lead the list.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:09.380
BYD captured 34.2% of China's June NEV export share, with Tesla in fourth place at 7.2%.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:15.640
The figures show Tesla maintaining a meaningful but secondary role in outbound shipments from the world's

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:22.640
largest EV market. BYD's lead reflects its broader product range and aggressive pricing in export

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:29.200
markets. Tesla vehicles assembled at the Shanghai plant still rank inside the top 7 despite the

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:35.960
broader dominance of domestic Chinese markets. Every one of Australia's top 7 electric vehicles in

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:42.840
recent sales data is a Chinese brand, including Tesla models built in China. The shift reflects

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:50.000
strong pricing and availability from BYD, MG, and others in the market. Tesla partnered with an

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.380
Australian lender to offer loans that guarantee a minimum future resale value for the vehicle.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:01.100
The structure aims to lower monthly payments and reduce buyer risk on depreciation.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:06.740
The program is designed to make new Tesla purchases more accessible by capping the financial

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:13.660
exposure tied to used market values. The partnership targets buyers concerned about residual values

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:20.060
in a fast-changing EV market. No specific loan terms or interest rate details were released in

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:25.860
the announcement. The arrangement covers new vehicle purchases and is positioned as a way to improve

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:32.100
affordability without changing vehicle pricing. Market share battles abroad contrast with product

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:39.320
updates Tesla is preparing for its core lineup. A longer wheelbase model Y is entering the US market

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:45.940
with an extended body. The change improves third row space and addresses complaints about tight legroom

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:53.320
for adults. No power train or battery alterations are involved. A filing indicates Tesla plans to

00:04:53.320 --> 00:05:00.080
reintroduce the model Y performance variant in China. The move would restore a higher power option

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.760
that had been absent from the lineup there. The refreshed version is expected to send more power

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.980
to the front wheels than earlier performance models. The update would bring the variant back

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:16.900
after a period without it in the Chinese market. No timing for customer deliveries was specified in

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:22.320
the filing. The change keeps the same overall platform while adjusting power distribution.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:28.980
Hardware refinements like the new model Y sit alongside software expansions already rolling out.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:34.920
Supervised full self-driving version 14 light has started deployment in South Korea.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:40.600
The update follows the incremental rollout pattern seen in other regions earlier this year.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:46.800
As autonomy features spread, Tesla is also extending its energy management reach beyond the car.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:53.900
Tesla home is a new AI platform that optimizes power wall and solar output in real time.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:06:00.540
The system decides whether to store, consume, or export energy based on utility rates and household

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:07.480
usage patterns. The goal is to cut bills through predictive control. Energy products and vehicle tech

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:14.700
both benefit from Tesla's vertical integration push. LG energy solution is expanding output at its

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:21.260
Nanjing plant to supply more cylindrical and pouch cells for Tesla lines. The added capacity supports

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:27.800
multiple production programs. Battery supply growth supports volume ambitions even as some markets

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:34.800
tighten robot taxi rules. One ex-post from analyst Pierre Faragou compared a Tesla to an iPhone.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:43.100
He noted that a $35,000 model 3 plus a $100 monthly subscription looks expensive only when viewed

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:49.620
strictly as a car. Once full self-driving capability is factored in, the vehicle becomes a tool for

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:55.760
stress-free daily transport. Faragou said two more quarters are needed to see where the technology

00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:01.960
heads. Tesla also amplified an owner note that the model-wise range, performance, and features

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:09.280
led the owner to drop an Aston Martin DBX-707 and a Porsche Taycan Turbo S from the fleet.

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:15.200
The post frames the model-wise as delivering comparable daily utility at lower cost.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:21.420
Separately, Tesla highlighted steer-by-wire and four-wheel steering as a core differentiator

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:25.340
that improves maneuverability without traditional mechanical linkages.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:31.300
Car and driver conducted a direct comparison between the Tesla model-wise performance and the

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:37.200
Polestar 4 dual motor performance plus. The test evaluates acceleration, handling,

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:42.120
range, and interior space between the two performance-oriented electric crossovers.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:47.480
Results will provide one of the first head-to-head data points for buyers choosing between

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:54.460
the updated Model Y and its newest European rival. The evaluation covers real-world driving dynamics

00:07:54.460 --> 00:08:00.800
on public roads and test tracks. No preliminary results have been released ahead of the full article.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:06.100
The match-up focuses on vehicles positioned at similar price and performance levels.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:13.060
NASA selected SpaceX's Falcon Heavy to launch the Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope in August.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:19.180
The mission aims to detect exoplanets and study dark energy with the telescope's wide-field

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:25.500
infrared instrument. The launch will mark another high-profile science payload carried by the heavy-lift

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:30.720
vehicle. The selection follows standard NASA procurement for large observatories requiring

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:36.300
substantial lift capacity. No alternate launch providers were named in the announcement.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:43.060
The telescope's primary goals center on infrared observations that require stable orbital insertion.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:48.040
Now, one thing worth watching is the regulatory pressure around robot axes.

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:54.080
State and federal regulators are raising hurdles that could delay or restrict deployment plans.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:09:00.040
The uncertainty centers on approval timelines for unsupervised operation and vehicle

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:06.280
requirements that differ across jurisdictions. Tesla's ability to scale the service depends on

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:12.820
clearing these regulatory gates in key markets. The outcome will determine whether the Miami test can

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:19.800
expand into a broader commercial network or remain geographically limited. The panoramic roof has

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:25.080
long forced to compromise between openness and efficiency because glass conducts heat and

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:31.660
transmits noise far more readily than insulated metal. Tesla's perforated multi-layer approach

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:36.340
attacks both problems at the material level by letting conditioned air move through the

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:41.020
pain itself rather than fighting the heat load after it has already entered the cabin.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:47.620
That single change removes the need for extra mass in acoustic liners or oversized compressors.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.420
Directly trimming the energy budget that otherwise reduces range on hot days.

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.640
The design also reveals a deeper manufacturing choice.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:02.780
Instead of sourcing a finished acoustic glass module from a supplier, Tesla is internalizing the

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:09.480
geometry, porosity, and HVAC integration. Owning those parameters lets the company tune whole

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:15.480
size, gap depth, and wall patterns for the exact noise spectrum each vehicle platform encounters.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:20.140
Something and off the shelf supplier is unlikely to optimize per model.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:26.500
The result is a part that simultaneously serves daylight admission, sound absorption, and climate

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:33.060
distribution, collapsing three separate systems into one structural element. Over time, the bigger

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:39.600
implication is cost per vehicle rather than any single efficiency gain. Every watt no longer

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:45.040
spent on extra cooling or sound deadening material is a watt that does not have to be generated,

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:51.500
stored, or paid for in battery capacity. When the same roof architecture can be adapted across

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:58.260
model Y, Cybertruck, and future platforms, the engineering investment amortizes across higher

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:03.720
volumes while the marginal cost of each additional vehicle stays lower than if those functions remain

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:10.900
discrete add-ons. Before we go, keep an eye on further Robotaxi test expansions and any updates

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:17.780
on the New Jersey bill, and that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today. TSLA closed at

